    <paragraph>Write the Equation of a Circle in Standard Form</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, write the standard form of the equation of the circle with the given radius and center $$\left( {0,0} \right).$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="17" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: 7</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 + y 2 = 49 x 2 + y 2 = 49$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="18" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: 9</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="19" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: $$\sqrt{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x 2 + y 2 = 2 x 2 + y 2 = 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="20" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: $$\sqrt{5}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, write the standard form of the equation of the circle with the given radius and center</paragraph>
    <exercise number="21" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: 1, center: $$\left( {3,5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( x - 3 ) 2 + ( y - 5 ) 2 = 1 ( x - 3 ) 2 + ( y - 5 ) 2 = 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="22" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: 10, center: $$\left( {-2,6} \right)$$</paragraph>
