    </exercise>
    <exercise number="23" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: $$2.5,$$ center: $$\left( {1.5,-3.5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( x - 1.5 ) 2 + ( y + 3.5 ) 2 = 6.25 ( x - 1.5 ) 2 + ( y + 3.5 ) 2 = 6.25$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="24" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Radius: $$1.5,$$ center: $$\left( {-5.5,-6.5} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, write the standard form of the equation of the circle with the given center with point on the circle.</paragraph>
