    <paragraph>Graph a Circle</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, ⓐ find the center and radius, then ⓑ graph each circle.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="29" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x + 5} \right)^{2} + \left( {y + 3} \right)^{2} = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ The circle is centered at $$(-5,-3)(-5,-3)$$ with a radius of 1. ⓑ</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="30" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x - 2} \right)^{2} + \left( {y - 3} \right)^{2} = 9$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="31" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {x - 4} \right)^{2} + \left( {y + 2} \right)^{2} = 16$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ The circle is centered at $$(4,-2)(4,-2)$$ with a radius of 4. ⓑ</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="32" has_solution="false">
